{"availability":"available","full":"martin-sicho/genui","name":"genui","description":"The backend services of the GenUI framework. The backend provides the REST API used for molecular generation, QSAR modelling and chemical space visualization.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":36,"forks":17,"created":"2019-11-29T15:49:21Z","updated":"2026-02-03T09:59:24Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://martin-sicho.github.io/genui/docs/index.html","topics":["chemical-space","cheminformatics","data-science","molecular-generation","qsar","rest-api","visualization","webapp"],"demo":"https://martin-sicho.github.io/genui/docs/index.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:45.168Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:45.168Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:45.168Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T13:01:45.168Z","stars":36,"forks":17}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The GenUI framework provides both API and GUI for molecular generators, QSAR modelling and chemical space visualization. This repository contains the implementation of the backend application used in the GenUI platform.","Molecular generators can be integrated as self-contained Python packages and their inputs, outputs and data storage can be managed through various REST API endpoints implemented in this repository. It is possible to upload bioactivity datasets and also download them from public sources. QSAR and generative models can be built from this data as well as 2D representations of chemical space. The GenUI web frontend uses the REST services implemented here to allow simpler access to all these features. You can find out more about how to extend and use the GenUI Python API in the documentation.","You can also directly deploy and test existing open source GenUI ecosystem as Docker images (more details here)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/martin-sicho/genui/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"557c8c640262b87cc4f822fb0dca42f0c7a96016a9213f95424c307ea958b7a2","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:45.334Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:45.334Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The GenUI framework provides both API and GUI for molecular generators, QSAR modelling and chemical space visualization. This repository contains the implementation of the backend application used in the GenUI platform.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/martin-sicho/genui/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"557c8c640262b87cc4f822fb0dca42f0c7a96016a9213f95424c307ea958b7a2","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/martin-sicho/genui/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:45.335Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-02-03T09:59:24Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/martin-sicho/genui/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:45.335Z","hash":"557c8c640262b87cc4f822fb0dca42f0c7a96016a9213f95424c307ea958b7a2","originalBytes":1535,"storedBytes":1535,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["genui","api","generators","molecular","about","any","application","chemical","contact","data","here","hesitate","implemented","license","python","qsar","rest","access","allow","appreciate","backend","bioactivity","both","built","collaborations","contains","contribute.","create","datasets","deploy","details","development","directly","distributed","docker","documentation","download","ecosystem","endpoints","existing","extend","feature","features.","feedback.","find","framework","frontend","generative","github","gui","how","images","implementation","inputs","integrate","integrated","interested","issue.","license.md","like","managed","mit","modelling","models","much","open","out","outputs","packages","platform","platform.","possible","problems","provides","public","questions","repository","repository.","representations","requests","self-contained","services","simpler","software","sourc